{
  "id": "thangyat",
  "name": "Thangyat (Thingyan satirical chant)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Burmese performance genre of rhymed satirical verse chanted by a lead performer and answered by a chorus, to the beat of traditional drums or a hsaing waing ensemble and interspersed with song and dance routines. Troupes perform during Thingyan, the water festival before the Burmese New Year in April, voicing social and political criticism. Thangyat was permitted again in 2013, after a ban imposed by the military government in 1989, on condition that troupes submit their verses in advance, and in 2019 members of the Peacock Generation troupe were sentenced to prison for a performance satirising the army. A generic membrane-drum card stands in for the drums.",
